{"term":"queue","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:8993644e106870a14d","definition":"A line of people, vehicles or other objects, usually one to be dealt with in sequence (i.e., the one at the front end is dealt with first, the one behind is dealt with next, and so on), and which newcomers join at the opposite end (the back).","example":"I was absent-minded at the moment and was last in the queue.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["line","lineup"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Commonwealth, Ireland, UK, uncommon","register":"Commonwealth, Ireland, UK, uncommon","wordFamily":["caudal","jump the queue","queueing theory","queue-jump","queue-jumper","queueless","quevée","cue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8b2c73da259c15ae79","definition":"A waiting list or other means of organizing people or objects into a first-come-first-served order.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["queue"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["caudal","jump the queue","queueing theory","queue-jump","queue-jumper","queueless","quevée","cue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:89632c6669fba60dd7","definition":"A data structure in which objects are added to one end, called the tail, and removed from the other, called the head (in the case of a FIFO queue). The term can also refer to a LIFO queue or stack where these ends coincide.","example":"2005, David Flanagan, Java in a Nutshell, p. 234,\nQueue implementations are commonly based on insertion order as in first-in, first-out (FIFO) queues or last-in, first-out queues (LIFO queues are also known as stacks).","pos":"noun","synonyms":["queue"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["caudal","jump the queue","queueing theory","queue-jump","queue-jumper","queueless","quevée","cue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:35450bd2c80e0ee191","definition":"An animal's tail.","example":"HESSE: Az., a lion, queue fourchée, rampt., barry of ten, arg. and gu., crowned, or, and holding in his dexter paw a sword, ppr., hilt and pommel, gold.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["queue"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["caudal","jump the queue","queueing theory","queue-jump","queue-jumper","queueless","quevée","cue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:342a1d2399ede78362","definition":"A men's hairstyle with a braid or ponytail at the back of the head, such as that worn by men in Imperial China.","example":"In the morning and evening, spruce Chinamen stroll about or chat at each other's doors, in blue trousers, white jacket, and a queue into which red silk is plaited till it reaches almost to their heels.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["queue"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"historical","wordFamily":["caudal","jump the queue","queueing theory","queue-jump","queue-jumper","queueless","quevée","cue"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queue#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d14f1ea4af1a66b6b0","definition":"To put oneself or itself at the end of a waiting line.","example":"Although there is a spacious circulating area beyond the platforms at Clacton, there is severe overcrowding on peak Saturdays; at times of pressure passengers have to queue out into the street [...]","pos":"